# A 32-bit element unpacked by `mov.b64 {x, y}, %rd` from a register a
# mov packed, `mov.b64 %rd, {a, b}`, is that element (PTX ISA §9.7.9.4),
# through a copy and with a sink, and the value its element register had
# at the pack. An unpack after a join of two packs, one of a different
# element count, one of a 64-bit product, one of an unpacked element and
# one of an immediate wider than 32 bits stay refused. A guarded pack is
# read as the last write, and a guard on its element is a bound.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/unpack.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_unpack
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 16–17 sectors (ideal 4)
CHECK-SAME: [16 * %tid.x + 512 * %ctaid.x + param_0]
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 16–17 sectors (ideal 4)
CHECK-SAME: [16 * %tid.x + param_1]
CHECK: kernel micro_unpack_join
CHECK: unknown: %r3 is one of `mov.b64`'s vector destinations
CHECK: kernel micro_unpack_halves
CHECK: unknown: %rs1 is one of `mov.b64`'s vector destinations
CHECK: kernel micro_unpack_wide
CHECK: unknown: %r2 is one of `mov.b64`'s vector destinations
CHECK: kernel micro_unpack_twice
CHECK: unknown: %rs2 is one of `mov.b32`'s vector destinations
CHECK: kernel micro_unpack_imm
CHECK: unknown: %r2 is one of `mov.b64`'s vector destinations
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 1 sector (ideal 1)
CHECK-SAME: [param_0 + 64]
CHECK: kernel micro_unpack_redefined
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 16–17 sectors (ideal 4)
CHECK-SAME: [16 * %tid.x + param_0]
CHECK: kernel micro_unpack_guarded
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B
CHECK-SAME: warp: 1 sector (ideal 1)
CHECK-SAME: [param_0]
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B (predicated)
CHECK-SAME: warp: <= 1 sector (ideal 1)
CHECK: global bytes: load 0 B, store <= 8 B
